# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Locally-built hydra binary (e.g. `go build -o hydra .`); mage builds to .mage/
/hydra

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Hydra remote-access auth key (secret; generated by `mage deploy:setup`)
/.hydra/deploy.toml

# Hydra per-user-per-project config override (untracked, non-secret)
/.hydra/config.local.toml

# Bundled sandbox helper binaries (pasta/bwrap) provisioned by `mage tools:ensure`
/.hydra/tools/

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Mage timestamp files
.mage
mage/mage_output_file.go

# Core dumps
core
core.*
# Stray root-level node_modules (tooling run from the repo root by mistake;
# the real one lives in web/)
/node_modules/

# Self-hosted webfonts (Iosevka, Iosevka Term, the Nerd Fonts symbol fallback).
# Not committed - `cd web && npm run build-fonts` (which `npm run build` runs
# first) fetches them from the upstream releases and subsets them into place.
# See web/scripts/build-fonts.ts.
/web/public/fonts/iosevka-*.woff2
/web/public/fonts/nerd-symbols-*.woff2
# The mirrored Google families (scripts/build-fonts.ts vendorGoogle).
/web/public/fonts/google.css
/web/public/fonts/google/
/web/.iosevka-build.json
